vcl: LOK idle jobs yield to the client's waiting requests

Writer's idle jobs (online spelling, autocomplete words, word count,
smart tags) stop when Application::AnyInput says input waits. The
headless backend answers only for timers, and Windows only for its
own message queue; neither asks the LOK client. A 14 MB DOCX spent
0.6 to 1.3 seconds in online spelling before the client's next
request ran (Ely SF.18). Patch 0007 did this for Aqua alone.

Application::AnyInput now returns true when the LOK any-input
callback reports a waiting request, then asks the backend as before.

diff --git a/vcl/source/app/svapp.cxx b/vcl/source/app/svapp.cxx
index 3034b7204..6df2bfe57 100644
--- a/vcl/source/app/svapp.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/app/svapp.cxx
@@ -565,6 +565,9 @@ sal_uInt16 Application::GetDispatchLevel()
 
 bool Application::AnyInput( VclInputFlags nType )
 {
+    // LOK: the client's waiting requests are input too.
+    if (comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive() && comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::anyInput())
+        return true;
     return ImplGetSVData()->mpDefInst->AnyInput( nType );
 }
 
